0199: AppleIPAppender stand-in for CommCenter (bluepdp)

CommCenter (no-baseband job, kept since 2026-11-23) makes an
ApplePDPHelperInterface; without an AppleIPAppender service its first
callStructMethod locks a mutex through NULL and CommCenter dies (SIGSEGV),
about half of its restarts. iokit/Kernel/arm/MiniIPAppender.cpp publishes
AppleIPAppender under IOResources with a user client that refuses every
method (kIOReturnUnsupported). The SIGSEGVs stop (0 in 10 min, cc5);
CommCenter still aborts every ~17 s on its baseband path (std::runtime_error
"Unable to communicate with AppleBaseband driver"), open. Started from bsd_init after the payload
install; bluepdp=0 leaves it out.

diff -ruN a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c
--- a/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c	2026-11-23 13:45:59
+++ b/bsd/kern/bsd_init.c	2026-11-23 13:46:28
@@ -959,6 +959,11 @@
 		extern void blueline_payload_install(void);
 		blueline_payload_install();
 	}
+	{
+		/* 0199: AppleIPAppender stand-in for CommCenter (iokit/Kernel/arm/MiniIPAppender.cpp) */
+		extern void MiniIPAppenderStart(void);
+		MiniIPAppenderStart();
